{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"afd01e1afdb0e3b5","type":"text","text":"How do I best start this?","x":-1380,"y":380,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"e196624f1fe033ea","type":"text","text":"Dan in the middle of planning an event for Minister Ama. Likely his name-day. Dan is hard at work, and shows his ability and station.","x":-1700,"y":500,"width":250,"height":220,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f2c9c451012f5c6e","type":"text","text":"Dan gets exiled right from the jump?\n\nOn one hand, this gets things rolling immediately. On the other, it might feel rushed, and we don’t get time to establish the status quo before we break it.","x":-1380,"y":500,"width":250,"height":340,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"968f8e0133082427","type":"text","text":"We can start with Dan being his cunning self, and strong-arming a prominent person. \n\nPros: Shows his character. Delivers a promise. Gets reader invested in the character.\n\nCons:  ","x":-1060,"y":504,"width":250,"height":496},
		{"id":"ee8b8e54039004b2","type":"text","text":"Old teahouse opening? Why do I even want to change this?","x":-1700,"y":816,"width":250,"height":164,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f4851e83961f41a2","type":"text","text":"What point is this in Dan’s life?","x":-1380,"y":-440,"width":250,"height":79},
		{"id":"b1923dcc0f4a6d2a","type":"text","text":"Dan is in a good spot, good enough for most people. He is the adopted (unofficial) son of a childless minister. (Minister Ama)\n\n\nThis isn’t enough. He isn’t necessarily ambitious, but he wants to be nobility to deserve and marry the woman he’s seeing (a princess of sorts)","x":-1380,"y":-140,"width":250,"height":440,"color":"4"},
		{"id":"aac801ccbf47c13b","type":"text","text":"He is a beggar.","x":-1380,"y":-260,"width":250,"height":83,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"7e43e90cd02b5f21","type":"text","text":"He is nothing, and a nobody. A commoner.","x":-1700,"y":-20,"width":250,"height":80,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"a089768969bfc643","type":"text","text":"He is the king of Meroun.","x":-1700,"y":100,"width":250,"height":83,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"5a16d28ca9a0e650","type":"text","text":"Comfortable. Safe. Trending up. ","x":-1700,"y":-260,"width":250,"height":83,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"f94f5e70003a16d1","type":"text","text":"He has everything he wants.","x":-1700,"y":-140,"width":250,"height":83,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"3dec97380430b2a4","type":"text","text":"Let’s do something that immediately portrays his low station to establish his primary motivation.","x":-1380,"y":1060,"width":250,"height":160},
		{"id":"efd1b87664561535","type":"text","text":"“The city of Meroun will starve to death, and no else dared admit it.”","x":-1380,"y":1280,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"6d0d4350f273194f","type":"text","text":"Dan is negotiating with a minister about something. What could it be?","x":-1380,"y":1460,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"5079ecd624f16089","type":"text","text":"Rice importation","x":-1540,"y":1740,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"1e6b9faf935c68aa","type":"text","text":"Use of warehouses","x":-1220,"y":1740,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"263021cf417a1022","type":"text","text":"Marriage w/ his daughter","x":-1540,"y":1840,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"1"},
		{"id":"588b1375ae3f5f4f","type":"text","text":"Money","x":-1220,"y":1840,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"234946894f25b74d","type":"text","text":"Something political","x":-1540,"y":1940,"width":250,"height":60,"color":"3"},
		{"id":"fce9fe1c70cc2e2d","type":"text","text":"What is their conflict?","x":-1380,"y":2120,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"628c0e9defe96aa4","type":"text","text":"Minister doesn’t respect Dan because he is of low birth. He isn’t subtle about this, unlike others","x":-1380,"y":2220,"width":250,"height":151},
		{"id":"193084833ecdb71a","type":"text","text":"How does Dan respond to this?","x":-1380,"y":2411,"width":250,"height":80},
		{"id":"235834252a212751","type":"text","text":"He doesn’t retaliate or show negative emotion. Instead he offers help. To fix one of his problems.","x":-1380,"y":2531,"width":250,"height":144},
		{"id":"1ef6d164347607ca","type":"text","text":"What problem?","x":-1380,"y":2711,"width":250,"height":60},
		{"id":"0d0dac4163d329ff","type":"text","text":"One of his sons is missing, but didn’t try too hard to find him because he has a much younger son that would be a better heir.","x":-1380,"y":2811,"width":250,"height":169},
		{"id":"6a014efdb44b47d7","type":"text","text":"Scene with the princess in Snowdrop Garden","x":-1380,"y":3100,"width":250,"height":120},
		{"id":"ca269de912fe3227","x":-1380,"y":3300,"width":250,"height":260,"type":"text","text":"Mislead the reader as though she was a courtesan, and Dan a simp. He calls her ‘My Princess’ \n\n“Romance can bloom in the unlikeliest of places.”"},
		{"id":"951b8525aedbb0b2","x":-1380,"y":3760,"width":250,"height":200,"type":"text","text":"At the end she says ‘she must leave,’ implying their time is up. Dan tries to haggle with her, but she insisted. (Really make Dan look like a simp fool)\n\n"},
		{"id":"4e33568000b592a3","x":-1380,"y":4020,"width":250,"height":360,"type":"text","text":"“Wait for me.”\n\n“Always, my dear.”\n\n“No, you don’t understand. I can see it—I’m getting somewhere. Give me a few more years and I will be worthy of your hand, my princess, and whatever else is attached.”"}
	],
